    "faq_section": {
      "type": "faq-section",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "I’ve tried strips and kits before and they didn't work. Why is this any different?",
            "sub_title": "<p>One-size-fits-all whitening fail because they assume all yellow teeth are the same. In reality, discoloration comes from four distinct root causes—plaque film, surface stains, deep stains, or thin enamel. If your yellowing is caused by thin enamel, traditional bleach will never work. We analyze your specific dental profile first to target the exact cause of your discoloration, not just surface symptoms.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why should I subscribe?",
            "sub_title": "<p>While you’ll see a visible lift in your first few sessions, whitening is a compounding process—especially if you're a first time whitener or have stubborn, deep-set yellow.</p><ul><li><strong>Compounding results:</strong> While the first 6 treatments clears off years of stains, for deeply yellow teeth or first-time whiteners, it’s just the foundation. Whitening builds on itself: each cycle safely penetrates deeper below the surface to break up stubborn, embedded stains that a single treatment can’t reach.</li><li><strong>Stop new stains before they set:</strong> Daily habits like coffee and tea continuously leave fresh stains behind. Regular refills clear that surface buildup every two months before it has time to bond with your enamel.</li><li><strong>Complete flexibility:</strong> You save <strong>40%</strong> on every order, with full control to pause, adjust delivery frequency, or cancel anytime in one click from your account.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Will this make my teeth sensitive?",
            "sub_title": "<p>No. Unlike generic whitening strips that use harsh, uniform peroxide levels for every mouth, your formula is calibrated to your specific sensitivity score. If you report sensitive teeth, we adjust the active whitening agents and balance them with enamel-fortifying ingredients to lift stains without triggering nerve pain or thinning your enamel.<br/><br/>If you experience any pain, we will send you an updated formula free of charge.</p><h3></h3>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does it work on crowns or veneers?",
            "sub_title": "<p>No. Whitening only works on natural teeth, so crowns, veneers and fillings stay the same shade.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long do results last?",
            "sub_title": "<p>The deep whitening effects last <strong>6 to 12 months</strong>. During that time, our formula actively strengthens your enamel and slows down future staining. That said, new stains from coffee, wine accumulate daily. Doing a brief touch-up every <strong>2 months</strong> clears away surface buildup before it can penetrate the enamel, keeping your teeth permanently bright without ever having to start over.</p><h4></h4>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4m3LPU": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What if my formula doesn’t work?",
            "sub_title": "<p>We guarantee shade improvement. Because your formula is built specifically for your teeth, we stand behind the outcome: if you complete your treatment and aren't thrilled with your results, our team will review your feedback, reassess your teeth, and formulate a new blend for free.</p><h4></h4>"
          }
        }
      },
